
# Task 5: Matrix Algebra and Matrix Operations

## 1. Objective

The aim is to use matrices in Python to rotate and resize a square.

## 2. Inputs

The program uses four points that form a square. It rotates the square by 45 degrees, makes it twice as wide, and increases its height by 1.5 times.

## 3. Mathematical Operations

The program uses rotation and scaling matrices to calculate the new coordinates of the square.

## 4. Original Output

The program produced the transformation matrix and new coordinates for the four corners of the square.

The determinant was 3.0.

## 5. Modified Input

I changed the rotation angle from 45 degrees to 90 degrees.

## 6. Observation

Changing the rotation angle from 45 degrees to 90 degrees changed the coordinates of the square. The determinant remained 3.0.

## 7. Interpretation

Matrices make it easier to rotate and resize objects by calculating their new coordinates.

## 8. Related Real-World Problem

Computer games use matrices to rotate and resize objects on the screen.

## 9. Assumptions

The object is represented by four points. The scaling values remain unchanged.

## 10. New Input Data

The rotation angle is changed to 90 degrees. The scaling values remain 2.0 and 1.5.

## 11. Output

The modified program produced new coordinates:

[[0.0, 0.0],
 [0.0, 2.0],
 [-1.5, 2.0],
 [-1.5, 0.0]]

The determinant remained 3.0.

## 12. Interpretation of the Modified Problem

The new coordinates show the changed position of the object after rotation and resizing. This is useful in computer graphics and animation.
